Summary: Things worth adding in Nethack
Keywords: nethack ideas


I'd like to see wands of fire and cold with expanded effects. Wands of
fire should evaporate water - perhaps for only a few rounds. WIth a wand
of fire you could cross a lake, for instance. A sophisticated enhancement
of this would be for the evaporated water to make steam vortices, and for
the water to flow back after a semi random number of turns. It would also
be nice to hide valuable items in the water - like a tin of smoked eel!

Wands of cold should freeze water into ice, also making a path. This ice
could melt, so it would have the same effect as the wand of fire. A wand
of cold should kill a steam vortex, but sometimes make icy monsters from
the water.

Are there any projectile-weapon Artifacts? There should be. Bows with
flaming arrows, for instance.

When you kill an Iron Golem or get rid of an iron ball, you're left with a
chain. There doesn't appear to be any use for this. Why not make it into
an artifact, with the power of binding a monster? Iron's traditionally
proof against magic, so binding an adjacent wizard or magic-using undead
could stop it using its magic powers until it freed itself.

Other posters have suggested that monsters should also take turns to wear
or remove armor. This is an excellent idea. On the subject of armor,
perhaps iron armor should also interfere with magic?

Useful additions to the spellbooks would be ones that catalogue rings,
gems or artifacts. Having one in your possession would mean that you
automatically recognise the objects it describes. This would be an
interesting enhancement, and it wouldn't make things too easy. Remember,
you'd need half a dozen different ones to be able to recognise everything,
and you need to possess it (or even read it) each time you come across an
unfamilar object.

I'd like to see more access to intrinsics. Is it possible to get magical
breathing apart from an amulet? I think every ability should be gainable
as an intrinsic. Perhaps we could have dealers who sell intrinsics? And
how about peddlers, travelling shopkeepers? They'd come up to you and
offer artifacts (probably highly enchanted/cursed) for reasonable sums.
Hey, did you hear about the travelling shopkeeper and the player's tame nymph?

I like the new effect from the scroll of fire, as well as the fireball
spell. This should be extended to wands and other spells, so that you have
a standard wand of cold, and a ball of cold. The latter would be more
powerful. ALternatively, give wands of fire, cold, and missile an area
effect, and keep lightning, striking and so forth as straight-line ones. 

I agree with other posters about bribing cops. What about dragons, though?
They're notoriously greedy. Oh yes, and it would interesting to Dragons'
Lairs as a counterpart to Magic Zoos. The Lairs could have objects instead
of gold, sort of like a shop with a nasty and powerful shopkeeper.
Actually, it should be a mixture of gold, gems and artifacts, just like
Smaug's.

The Crysknife isn't much use anymore, not with named weapons so easily
accessible. I think it should be more powerful or possess some other
useful properties. Say, automatic lighting. 

Quickies: Rings of Intangibility, Spells of wall-walking, magic ladders,
ropes (from rope golems) that bind creatures when thrown, timed bombs,
portable holes.

